<report>
<title>McNemar and exact (Liddell) test for a paired fourfold table</title>

<p><b>Input table:</b></p>
<table>
<tr><td><in>tab_a1</in></td><td><in>tab_b1</in></td></tr>
<tr><td><in>tab_a2</in></td><td><in>tab_b2</in></td></tr>
</table>

<p>Uncorrected Chi<sub>2</sub> = <inu>chi</inu> (1 DF)  <pval><inp>chi_p</inp></pval><br />
Yates' continuity corrected Chi<sub>2</sub> = <inu>yates_chi</inu> (1 DF)  <pval><inp>yates_chi_p</inp></pval></p>

<p><b>After Liddell (1983):</b><br />
Point estimate of relative risk (R') = <in>risk</in></p>

<p><ci>Exact <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></ci></p>

<p>F = <inu>f</inu><br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>tail_2</inp></pval></p>
<block name="r_prime">

<p><warn>R' is significantly different from unity</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
